// title: "Piece and assembly identity migration"
// summary: "Map deliberately renamed subject IDs to their original recipe identities and recorded names without reallocating numeric game resources or rewriting historical evidence."
//
// Used when: Maintained tools must relate deliberately renamed piece or assembly IDs to original recipes, historical evidence identities, or files in a previous installation.
// Read by: scp.subject_identity._indexes() and its canonical/legacy identity helpers; installation, observation, connectivity, verification-fixture, and geometry lookup code use those helpers at declared boundaries.
// Updated by: A maintainer during an explicitly authorized naming migration, recording each old/current identity and the source-backed reason; normal builds and documentation refreshes do not regenerate it.
// Affects: Alias resolution, recipe-to-folder lookup, and upgrade identity comparisons without changing numeric game IDs; recorded names are historical, and current display names come from registered piece or assembly definitions.
// Reference: custom-pieces/docs/NAMING_CONVENTIONS.md explains identity migrations and which permanent identities must remain stable.
